    "hint": "Much dietary sodium comes from processed and prepared foods; label comparison helps identify sources.",
    "e": "Choosing lower-sodium packaged foods and reducing salty condiments can meaningfully lower intake. Sea salt generally contains similar sodium by weight, and potassium-based salt substitutes may be unsafe for some people with kidney disease or medications.",
    "source": "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/salt-reduction"
